.TH LIBEASYMCP2221 3 "September 2026" "libeasymcp2221" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
libeasymcp2221 \- C library for MCP2221 USB-to-I2C/GPIO bridges

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221.h>
.B #include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221_constants.h>

.BI "mcp2221_error_code_t mcp2221_open_simple(uint16_t " vid ", uint16_t " pid ","
.BI "                                          int " devnum ", const char *" usbserial ","
.BI "                                          int " i2c_speed_hz ", mcp2221_t **" out_dev ");"
.BI "void mcp2221_close(mcp2221_t *" dev ");"
.fi

Link with:
.BR "pkg-config --cflags --libs libeasymcp2221"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B libeasymcp2221
library is a C port of the EasyMCP2221 Python module for Microchip
MCP2221/MCP2221A USB-to-I2C/GPIO bridge chips. It exposes a C-style API with
explicit device handles and
.B mcp2221_error_code_t
return values instead of Python classes and exceptions.

Key capabilities include:
.IP \[bu] 2
Opening and closing MCP2221 devices by VID/PID, index or USB serial.
.IP \[bu] 2
I2C master read/write operations with explicit transfer kinds and timeouts.
.IP \[bu] 2
SMBus and I2C-slave convenience helpers.
.IP \[bu] 2
GPIO read/write, GPIO polling and pin-function configuration.
.IP \[bu] 2
ADC, DAC, clock, IOC, SRAM and flash settings helpers.
.IP \[bu] 2
Hardware/firmware revision reporting and explicit MCP2221 reset support.
.IP \[bu] 2
USB enumeration settings including Remote Wake-up and CDC serial-number
enumeration.

.SH API NAMING
The public version 2 API uses the
.B mcp2221_*
function prefix,
.B mcp2221_*_t
type names and
.B MCP2221_*
constant and macro prefix.

Compatibility aliases and unprefixed public headers from the 1.x series were
removed in version 2. See
.B MIGRATION.md
when upgrading an existing application.

.SH REVISION AND RESET
.B mcp2221_revision()
reports the MCP2221 hardware and firmware major/minor revision bytes through
.BR mcp2221_revision_t .

.B mcp2221_reset()
sends the MCP2221 reset command. After a successful reset, close the existing
device handle, wait for USB re-enumeration and open the device again.
libeasymcp2221 does not automatically wait for or reopen a reset device.

.SH USB CDC CONFIGURATION
.B mcp2221_usb_set_cdc_serial_enabled()
stages whether the MCP2221 CDC interface enumerates with its serial number.
Persist the staged value with
.BR mcp2221_flash_save_config()
and re-enumerate the device before expecting the host-visible setting to change.
The corresponding getter is
.BR mcp2221_usb_get_cdc_serial_enabled() .

UART payload data is not transported by the libeasymcp2221 HID API. Once the
CDC interface is enumerated, applications use the operating system's normal
serial-device interface for UART traffic.

.SH RETURN VALUES
Most functions return
.B MCP2221_ERR_OK
on success or another
.B mcp2221_error_code_t
value on failure. Functions that return payload lengths use output parameters.
Use
.B mcp2221_error_code_to_string()
to convert error codes to symbolic strings.

.SH RESOURCE OWNERSHIP
Successful
.B mcp2221_open*()
calls store an owned handle in the caller-provided output pointer. The handle
must be released with
.BR mcp2221_close() .

.B mcp2221_smbus_init()
borrows an existing MCP2221 handle when one is supplied. Otherwise it opens its
own handle, which is released by
.BR mcp2221_smbus_close() .

.SH SMBUS BLOCK SIZE
.B MCP2221_I2C_SMBUS_BLOCK_MAX
is 255 for EasyMCP2221 compatibility. The compatibility helpers use a one-byte
length field and treat the constant as the maximum payload length. This is
larger than the classic 32-byte SMBus block limit; applications that require
strict SMBus behavior should cap block payloads at 32 bytes themselves.

.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221.h>
#include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221_constants.h>

int main(void) {
    mcp2221_t *dev = NULL;
    mcp2221_error_code_t err =
        mcp2221_open_simple(MCP2221_DEV_DEFAULT_VID,
                            MCP2221_DEV_DEFAULT_PID,
                            0, NULL, 100000, &dev);
    if (err != MCP2221_ERR_OK)
        return 1;

    mcp2221_close(dev);

    return 0;
}
.fi

.PP
.BR mcp2221_open_simple ()
applies the requested I2C speed during initialization, so a second
.BR mcp2221_i2c_set_speed ()
call is not required.

